er explicit approval does Foreman receive dispatch for M1 pilot (`p3-socs-01..06`).\n# Current State: AJAMIX\n\n## As Of\n\n2026-07-13\n\n## Current Truth\n\n- **P6 Basic Science and the full Basic Science P3-P6 arc are CLOSED at 309 live modules.** The approved Nigeria-first/global-enriched source `tools/p6-batch/p6-bsci.json` contains exactly `p6-bsci-01..15`. The guarded merge on 2026-07-13 moved 294→309, preserved every pre-existing module object and every non-module top-level field, passed the 15-module structure/hook/redundancy gates, passed the full app validator at 309, and proved idempotent. The approved general pulley phrase is `na'urar dabaran igiya`. See `tasks/2026-07-13-p6-bsci-guarded-merge-report.md`. Image generation remains paused by user direction.\n- **P5 Basic Science hybrid: CLOSED 2026-07-11 — 15/15 modules, 294 total runtime modules.** New band (`p5-bsci-01..15`): environment/pollution, waste/recycling, skeleton/joints, pollination, rocks, acids/bases, materials/drawing instruments, vehicle safety (progression beyond `p4-bsci-20`), energy conversion, heat/temperature, simple circuits, magnets, nutrients (progression beyond `p4-bsci-21`), diseases/prevention, drug-awareness safety. One hook-lint defect found and fixed directly (`p5-bsci-13`: `kwai`→`ƙwai`). All uncertain terminology (skeleton/bone/joint, pollination/fertilisation, temperature/thermometer, circuit, magnet, nutrient-deficiency, communicable/non-communicable disease) handled via descriptive Hausa, none invented. All safety-sensitive modules (acids/bases, circuits, drug-awareness) independently read in full — adult-only handling, no operational/unsafe content, non-stigmatizing language confirmed. All 279 pre-existing modules confirmed byte-identical. Merged via `tools/p5-batch/apply-p5-bsci.mjs`. See `SESSION_NOTES.md` 2026-07-11 entry. **Pending**: image/diagram-needs manifest for this band (new standing request, not yet produced).\n- **P4 Basic Science hybrid additions: CLOSED 2026-07-11 — 21/21 modules, 279 total runtime modules.** Six new appended modules (`p4-bsci-16..21`: temporary/permanent changes, plant/animal life-cycle comparison, digestion/teeth, sound, vehicles/safe tech use, nutrition/healthy growth) built and merged; `p4-bsci-01..15` confirmed byte-identical throughout (zero changes, per the standing ruling that all 15 were already approved). `p4-bsci-18`/`p4-bsci-21` kept as separate modules per explicit user ruling (digestion/teeth vs nutrition, avoiding one ambiguous term across stomach/abdomen/intestine). All structural, quiz, redundancy, hook-lint, terminology (`gatari` confirmed absent, `sandar da ke tsakiya` used for axle), and safety gates independently verified — full content read directly, not sampled. Merged via `tools/p4-batch/apply-p4-bsci-appended.mjs`. See `SESSION_NOTES.md` 2026-07-11 entry and `tasks/2026-07-11-p4-bsci-appended-builder-brief.md`.\n- **Math-arc redundancy review: CLOSED 2026-07-11 — content clean; decimal sentence-splitting defect fixed in the development gate.** The 7 findings on `p5-maths-13`/`p6-maths-08/09/11` were confirmed false positives from a bug in `tools/p1-batch/check-within-module-redundancy.mjs`'s sentence-splitter (it treated a decimal point inside a number like `3.45` or `0.25` as a sentence terminator). Fixed the splitter (decimal-point protection via placeholder, restored after split; genuine sentence boundaries including Hausa `?`/`!` and plain-number-then-sentence unaffected); added `tools/p1-batch/test-redundancy-splitter.mjs` (10 regression fixtures, all pass); documented in `tools/p1-batch/README.md`. `--ids=` scoped run and full-file scan (`app/content.json`, 273 modules) now both report **zero findings**. `app/content.json` untouched (byte-identical, SHA-256 confirmed) — dev-tool-only change. See `SESSION_NOTES.md` 2026-07-11 entries.\n- **P3 Basic Science hybrid enrichment CLOSED 2026-07-11.** Applied the canonical map's P3 finding (zero SEMANTIC_REPLACEMENT entries needed) as 12 OBJECTIVE_PRESERVING_ENRICHMENT patches (`p3-bsci-01,03,05,07,08,09,10,11,12,13,14,15`) plus one new appended module `p3-bsci-16` (\"Plant Parts and Functions — Deeper Study\", approved by user this session, redundancy-checked against `p2-bsci-02` with zero overlap). `p3-bsci-02/04/06` are confirmed untouched (explicit KEEP rulings). `app/content.json` now at **273 modules**. Merged via `tools/p3-batch/apply-p3-bsci-hybrid.mjs`. See `tasks/2026-07-10-p3-bsci-hybrid-builder-brief.md` and `tasks/2026-07-11-p3-bsci-hybrid-candidate-report.md`. P4 Basic Science needs no hybrid dispatch at all (canonical map: zero changes across all 15 of its modules). P5/P6 Basic Science hybrid work is the next candidate, not yet authorized.\n- **P1 Basic Science within-module redundancy fix CLOSED 2026-07-10.** Live-file re-verification (never trust a carried-over defect list) found only 5 modules with real findings — `p1-bsci-02/03/07/09/14` — each with one duplicate/near-duplicate sentence in `textExplanationHa` only. Dispatched a narrowly-scoped Codex brief, independently verified the resulting patch (scope diff, redundancy checker, hook-lint), and merged via a new guarded script `tools/p1-batch/apply-p1-bsci-redundancy-patch.mjs`. `app/content.json` unchanged at 272 modules. Pre-existing out-of-scope Math-arc redundancy findings (`p5-maths-13`, `p6-maths-08/09/11`) remain unfixed and unscheduled. See `tasks/2026-07-10-p1-bsci-redundancy-fix-brief.md` and `tasks/p1-bsci-redundancy-report.md`.\n- **P1 band-wide content-quality hotfix CLOSED 2026-07-10.** All 37 prior Math/Social Studies filler replacements (`p1-maths-02..24`, `p1-socs-02..15`) were independently compared to their surrounding module text; all were redundant and rewritten with distinct topic-relevant value. Basic Science residuals were fixed: `kaɗawa` (`p1-bsci-10`), `hanci` pause answer (`p1-bsci-04`), `ɗanɗano` (`p1-bsci-05`), and the wheel-and-axle terminology (`p1-bsci-13`). `gatari` was ruled out because reliable dictionary evidence defines it as an axe; `sandar da ke tsakiya` is now the consistent learner-facing axle description. The reusable exact/normalized within-module redundancy gate lives at `tools/p1-batch/check-within-module-redundancy.mjs` and passed for the 41 edited modules. See `tasks/2026-07-10-p1-final-content-quality-closure-report.md`.\n- User acceptance: verified-output control governs this builder-first work; Codex may build when Claude is unavailable. Do not rerun or reopen P1 without a concrete regression. Future Codex dispatches must keep the detailed report path separate from `--output-last-message`.\n- **P2 Basic Science migration-safe hybrid candidate BUILT source-only 2026-07-10.** The candidate preserves all live `p2-bsci-01..15` IDs/objectives, keeps `p2-bsci-08` (Five Senses), provides only 8 approved editorial/objective-preserving enrichment patches, and adds exactly `p2-bsci-16..19` as a standalone batch. `app/content.json` is still 268 modules. Await Foreman content ruling before guarded application or merge work. See `tasks/2026-07-10-p2-bsci-hybrid-candidate-report.md`.\n\n- **M1, M2, M3, M4, and M5 are all complete and merged. The entire P3-P6 Mathematics content-build workstream is COMPLETE.** `/Users/muhammadbamalli/Documents/ajamix/app/content.json` verified at **238 modules** (148 + 18 M2 + 24 M3 + 24 M4 + 24 M5).\n- Terminology locks: P4 house standard (`desimal`, `perimita`, `siffar rektangul`/`rektangul`, `goma-goma`, `ɗari-ɗari`, `yanki`, `kusurwa madaidaiciya`); P5 house standard — LCM/HCF (`mafi ƙaramin ninki na gari`, `ninki na gari`/`ninkaye na gari`, `mafi girman mai raba gari`, `mai raba gari`/`masu raba gari`), fractions (`lambar sama`, `lambar ƙasa`, `kashi masu ƙima ɗaya`, `lambar ƙasa ta gari`, `lambobin ƙasa na gari`, `ninkawa a giciye`, `kashi`), decimals/percentages (`desimal`, `alamar desimal`, `matsayi na goma-goma`, `matsayi na ɗari-ɗari`, `kashi cikin ɗari`, `percent`), ratio/geometry/statistics (`rasiyo